---
---

<section data-testid="evaluation" id="evaluation" class="py-10 lg:py-14">

	<div class="sticky top-16 z-40 bg-white/95 pb-5 backdrop-blur-sm dark:bg-black/95">
		<p class="mb-2 inline-block rounded-md bg-orange/10 px-3 py-1 font-monospace text-base font-bold text-orange lg:text-lg">04 — Evaluation</p>
		<h2 class="font-monospace text-3xl text-black dark:text-white lg:text-5xl">
			What we tested and what we found
		</h2>
	</div>
	<p class="mb-8 max-w-xl text-sm leading-loose text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
		Two rounds of in-person user testing (heuristic evaluation + think-aloud sessions). 4–5 participants per round. No prior exposure to the prototype.
	</p>

	<!-- Round 1 -->
	<div class="mb-8">
		<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3">
			<div class="flex h-7 w-7 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-orange text-xs font-bold text-white">1</div>
			<div>
				<p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange">Round 1</p>
				<h3 class="font-monospace text-lg font-bold text-black dark:text-white">Heuristic Evaluation + User Testing</h3>
			</div>
		</div>
		<p class="mb-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-gray-500">
			Evaluated on the wireframe / medium-fidelity prototype using Nielsen's heuristics.
		</p>
		<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-900">
			<table class="w-full text-xs">
				<thead>
					<tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
						<th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange">Task</th>
						<th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange">Issue</th>
						<th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange">Recommendation</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 dark:divide-gray-800">
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Create an event</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">After creating, event card on Home tab was not tappable — users had to navigate to My Events. <em>Violates: Consistency and Standards.</em></td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">All event cards made tappable, linking to event detail page from any screen.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Create an event</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">"Vibe" label and options (Quiet / Casual / Deep) too abstract. <em>Violates: Match Between System and Real World.</em></td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Renamed to "Dining Atmosphere"; options: Quiet Meal / Casual Hangout / Deep Conversation.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Find and join an event</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Participant avatars looked clickable but did nothing — users expected profile info on tap.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Made avatars clickable to display participant profile details.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Find and join an event</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Keyboard did not appear automatically when tapping the search bar.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Keyboard now appears immediately on search bar tap.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Communicate in chatroom</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Toggling "Mute Notifications" had no visible change. <em>Violates: Visibility of System Status.</em></td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Added pinned notice at top of chatroom showing key event info for all participants.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Login &amp; manage profile</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Error message on failed login not visually prominent — easy to overlook. <em>Violates: Visibility of System Status.</em></td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Redesigned with stronger contrast and clearer placement.</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- Round 2 -->
	<div class="mb-8">
		<div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-3">
			<div class="flex h-7 w-7 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-orange text-xs font-bold text-white">2</div>
			<div>
				<p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange">Round 2</p>
				<h3 class="font-monospace text-lg font-bold text-black dark:text-white">Heuristic Evaluation + User Testing</h3>
			</div>
		</div>
		<p class="mb-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-gray-500">
			Evaluated on the high-fidelity prototype. Heuristic evaluation surfaced structural issues; think-aloud sessions with 4–5 new participants followed.
		</p>

		<p class="mb-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400">Heuristic Evaluation</p>
		<div class="mb-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-900">
			<table class="w-full text-xs">
				<thead>
					<tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
						<th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange">Task</th>
						<th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange">Issue</th>
						<th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange">Recommendation</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 dark:divide-gray-800">
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Cancel and Edit Event</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Users entering from Home had no way to cancel or edit — had to go to My Events. Limits flexibility of use.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Added Cancel and Edit buttons directly on the event detail page regardless of entry point.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">View Event details</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Only a small "›" button was tappable. Conflicts with proximity principle.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Retained "›" as visual cue but expanded entire event card as the tappable area.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Communicate in chatroom — send message</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Chat input field positioned beneath keyboard, deviating from standard mobile patterns.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Input field repositioned directly above keyboard.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Newly established chatroom — edge case</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">No empty state design for a new chatroom with no messages or participants yet.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Added empty chatroom state to represent real post-creation scenarios.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Login &amp; manage profile</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Login &amp; Security screen had no entry point for help or support.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Added Help &amp; Support button on the Login &amp; Security page.</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>

		<p class="mb-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400">User Testing</p>
		<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-900">
			<table class="w-full text-xs">
				<thead>
					<tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
						<th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange">Task</th>
						<th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange">Issue</th>
						<th class="px-4 py-2.5 text-left font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-orange">Recommendation</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 dark:divide-gray-800">
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Create Event — preferences</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">"Budget" ambiguous (total vs. per-person?). "Group Size" unclear if creator counted.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Renamed to "Budget/Person"; added hint "incl. yourself" to Group Size.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Communicate in chatroom — report user</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Once a report reason was selected, users couldn't modify it without restarting.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Users can now change selected reason before submission.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Communicate in chatroom — view user</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Could tap others' avatars but NOT "You" to view own profile — had to navigate away.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Tapping "You" now opens own profile preview from within the chatroom.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">Login &amp; manage profile</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Confirmation screens lacked polish — hard to recognise completed actions.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Redesigned with clearer card layout and subtle highlight background.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-black dark:text-white">View Participants / User Profile</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Only part of participant list was clickable; avatars missing from list.</td>
						<td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Added avatars for all participants; made every participant clickable.</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- Notable findings -->
	<div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
		<div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-50 p-4 dark:bg-gray-900">
			<p class="mb-1 text-2xl font-bold text-orange">16</p>
			<p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">total issues surfaced across 2 evaluation rounds</p>
		</div>
		<div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-50 p-4 dark:bg-gray-900">
			<p class="mb-1 text-sm font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">Label clarity</p>
			<p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">most recurring friction — small wording changes had outsized impact on user confidence</p>
		</div>
		<div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-50 p-4 dark:bg-gray-900">
			<p class="mb-1 text-sm font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">Navigation consistency</p>
			<p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">users expected the same action regardless of which screen they entered from</p>
		</div>
		<div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-50 p-4 dark:bg-gray-900">
			<p class="mb-1 text-sm font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">Safety features</p>
			<p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">report flow and profile previews were expected even when not prompted</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
